+## Resolve the model and reasoning defaults
+
+When the caller specifies a model or reasoning setting, pass that choice explicitly.
+Otherwise, omit `--model`, `--models`, `--reasoning-mode`, `--reasoning-effort`, and
+`--browser-thinking-time` so Oracle resolves the configured defaults. For MCP,
+omit the corresponding optional fields. Examples below inherit configuration;
+they do not recommend a particular model.
+
+Inspect the exact invocation with `--dry-run full` from the intended working
+directory. Confirm the resolved model before submitting, since project settings
+can override the user model. To inspect user defaults, read only the model,
+reasoning and browser-selection fields in `${ORACLE_HOME_DIR:-$HOME/.oracle}/config.json`;
+keep credentials and unrelated configuration out of logs. Inherit API reasoning
+from `reasoningMode`/`reasoningEffort`, and browser selection from
+`browser.thinkingTime`/`browser.modelStrategy`. If the caller requested configured
+defaults but the preview conflicts with them, resolve that conflict before sending.
+Use established configuration and authorization without asking the caller to
+select the same model again. Ask when a required choice remains unresolved.
+
